Z||000026||annieL||09-08-2001||09:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B> [QUOTE]Originally posted by annieL:<BR>[b]With the advancement of Science I really do not think that having the wrong person is as much of an issue as it was before. <P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Your reply is what concerns me.<BR>"....really do not "THINK" that having the wrong person "IS AS MUCH" of an issue as it was before." <BR>I understand what you're saying, and there are a lot of worthless people on death row that are probably guilty, but if we and OUR 'justice' system are going to take a persons life, there better not be any "I think" involved.  AS MUCH of an issue today ...would make me feel pretty mad if someone were fixing to stick a needle in my arm for something I KNEW I didn't do. We have to be absolutly sure. 'Beyond a reasonable doubt' don't help much once a person is dead.<BR>Excuse the caps, they aren't in anger, I just don't know how to reply with bold face font.[/B][/QUOTE]<P>I apologize. I DO not think that it is an issue. I know that most people on death row are guilty, there may be a "small" (and I mean very small) fraction of innocent people. <P>I am not angry either so please do not take it that way. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
