Z||000030||annieL||09-08-2001||11:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>fla death row has had to let go way too many people THAT DIDNOT DO IT for me to think the state is anywhere near good enuff at picking only the guilty to kill. no amount of reviews is too much in life or death cases.<BR>pluss how many get framed see local news about 13 cops who killed and then planted guns on their unarmed victoms, but now the FBI got them , think any of these killer cop will face death??  mob hit men make deals to walk away only the poor are ever killed by the state.<BR>look at what kind of states still kill around the world, china is the only one to out kill usa.<BR>IF IT IS WRONG TO KILL, IT IS WRONG TO KILL KILLERS TOOO.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First off the state picks peers to determine if someone is guilty. The state makes it's case and if enough evidence points towards the accused then they are guilty. In most states those peers also pick the punishment.<P>And I myself have never seen 13 police officers frame someone and plant evidence. <P>Also the government will make deals with mobsters to get to them to give up "bigger" mobsters. Maybe not always right but if you don't have a boss can a mafia family survive? (I think I have been watching way too many mobster movies) <P>||||reg||1
