Z||000050||Urchin||09-10-2001||03:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by beer_stud_21:<BR><B>Urchin,<P>   As for the fact that the murderers get out of jail and kill more innocent people.  That point is moot.  Anyone who has commited a crime punisable by the death penalty would never be let out on parole should the death penalty be done away with<P>-marlin</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, the comments I made earlier were partly inspired by a show I recently saw on TLC.  I can't remember the guys name for the life of me, but he had killed a young girl at the age of 16.  He was released from prison after 6 yrs.  After being released, he was in and out of prison for a second time. (I can't remember the charges, I wasn't paying 100% attention.)  But after his second release, he ended up being jailed for a third time (this time for life).  All in all he murdered 18 people that they new of.  Now, again, I am not saying I support the death penalty, but you have to consider the fact that 17 of the 18 could have been saved if he had been dealt with accordingly. (not necessarily by death).  This is not the only time I have heard of this happenning.  I am not up to date on all of the laws in this area, but whatever happened to life sentence without the possibility of parole?  Obviously the man I mentioned was young at the time of his first conviction, but that is not so in all cases.  Even so, should age be a deciding factor when sentencing for a crime of this nature.  Some are tried as adults, yes, but not all.  Actually, does anyone know how they determine whether to try the assailant as a juevenile or an adult?  ...more thoughts...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000051||Leper||09-10-2001||03:59 AM||||I'm for it. But personaly, I believe the current reasons people get the death penalty are more political rather than if the person is actually guilty of the crime or not. So I don't think that it's right to do it as of now.<P>I also believe that the media should not be allowed to report on felony cases. At least to the point where names are used.||||reg||1
Z||000052||Butter||09-10-2001||11:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierowrecker:<BR><B> He who is without sin, cast the first stone...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>an eye for an eye...<P>I believe modern technology should be used to confirm such a profane action.  There are a lot of good people called "Dead Veterans" that give us the right to argue this.  So if one innocent person is executed and proven to be innocent after the fact, then he should inter "Dead Veteran" status.<P>"Today is a good day to die"<BR>Translated, I am willing to die for what I believe in.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000053||RobertVol||09-10-2001||03:59 PM||||First of all, I saw some pretty good points posted on this subject. I did not read all of them so If I go over something already covered, I apologize.<P>1st of all..I am for the Death Penalty.<P>It really does not matter what the punishment is....if you dont do the crime, you dont have to worry about the time. <P>I have NEVER even been concerned with being mistakened for a Murderer. Dont know why. Maybe its the company I keep.<P>My point is ....<P>Even if the people who are arrested are innocent in some super rare instance, They are usually up to know good for something else. Maybe not as drastic as murder, but something is amiss. Cops dont go down the street and just pick people out and say ..your a murderer. Clean living, honest people, rarely get arrested even on accident for murder. "Birds of a feather flock together" and "if you play with dirt you will get dirty" are statements that come to mind. You may say, "well thats no reason for them to be excecuted". but then again in other countries, you can get killed for alot less!  Maybe we should quit worrying so much about his rights than how he should repay for his gross misconduct.<P><BR>How many people in here can honestly say they have a lost an IMMEDIATE family member and would not want the death penalty for the killer? Its easy for us to say its wrong its Politically incorrect (Which by the way is a bunch of crap). But we have not had something taken from us. The person who posted earlier seems to share a different opinion than the majority because they have been hurt by some punk animal who decided to take soemones life. <P>And back to the first statement I made. <BR>If you live honestly and dont break the law and follow the rules, how many of you really are scared you will be arrested for murder and put to death? I would say very slim ..<P>When I was 16, I was at a party and went with this guy on a beer run. We were both drunk. Got up to the store bought the beer and got back in the car. We headed back to the party. Well the cops pulled him over and come to find out the car was stolen...<P>I did not know it was stolen. BUT I was charged for GTA.. Well if they would have convicted me I would have been charged for a crime I did not commit. But you know..I was guilty of alot worse! I condoned a driver of getting in car DRUNK and being just as deadly as a murderer. Thank god he did not hit anyone and kill them, but It proves the point that I was not guilty of the GTA charge but was guilty of alot more in my opinion. If you think these guys who get charged with Murder but are innocent were purely innocent ..I would think again..<BR>They were in the wrong place at the wrong for other reasons in alot of cases. <P>In my opinion our country is still to soft on crime. I remember the story of the kid who went to Singapore and stole a sign or whatever and got cained....All of the United States was pissed off..thats wrong to punish such a nice kid and all that BLAH BLAH BLAH CRAP!<P>Then he gets arrested for Public intoxication when he gets back! He was punk and we should have let him get his ass cained a little. Maybe next time he would consider other peoples property.<P>Again. My opinion is I am for it. In my opinion its not used enough. what gets me is when we dont even need a trial..hundreds of people see a man get killed by someone. forget the courts. Have a trial in streets of the people FOR REAL. And if guilty by his peers..Shoot him on the spot. That will stop alot of this Gang and Riot crap real quick,<BR>OOOPPPPSSS<P>I also agree with the press should be kept out of it! Anyone who thiks the news just reports the news is really blind the world. <P>Sorry for Rambling...<P>But again good points from everyone, just wanted share mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks for the space.<p>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000054||Fierowrecker||09-10-2001||09:56 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Butter:<BR><B> an eye for an eye...<P>I believe modern technology should be used to confirm such a profane action.  There are a lot of good people called "Dead Veterans" that give us the right to argue this.  So if one innocent person is executed and proven to be innocent after the fact, then he should inter "Dead Veteran" status.<P>"Today is a good day to die"<BR>Translated, I am willing to die for what I believe in.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"An eye for an eye."<BR>Nice, but not relavent...<BR>Jesus clarafied the old testament... <BR>When Jesus said "He who is without sin, cast the first stone." He was reinforcing the "Thou shalt not kill." and it delt directly with crime and criminals...<BR>An eye for an eye, did not mean take a life, if another took a life, for you become as the killer...<BR>Instead, drive the wicked from society (incarseration)...<BR>As to "Today is a good day to die." it's a nice line from a movie...<BR>Dieing for what you believe in, that is what a martyr is...<BR>I would much rather live by God's law, than any law man can devise, as man's law is always flawed...<BR>After all, God has it covered with 10 laws...<BR>11 if you count "Do unto others"...<BR>crash...<p>[This message has been edited by Fierowrecker (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
