Z||000063||Voytek||09-12-2001||01:33 PM||||I hope you mean swaying people's opinions TOWARDS the death penalty.  All those who supported the terrorists (financially and otherwise) should be put to death so we may prevent future tragedies, such as the one yesterday, from ever happening again.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000064||Boomtastic||09-12-2001||06:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierowrecker:<BR><B>Death is not a deterent to crime, nor is any form of punishment...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, I disagree. Let's look at it this way - why don't you or I kill people? We are afraid of the consequences that follow when we are caught. If you know about, or care about, the consequences prior to commiting the crime, most people would be hesitant about commiting the crime in the first place.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000065||Urchin||09-12-2001||06:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Boomtastic:<BR><B> Actually, I disagree. Let's look at it this way - why don't you or I kill people? We are afraid of the consequences that follow when we are caught. If you know about, or care about, the consequences prior to commiting the crime, most people would be hesitant about commiting the crime in the first place.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't think I agree with that.  Consequences aren't what keep me from killing someone.  I simply know that it is wrong and and am not the type of person to commit such an act.  ...if someone has intentions on killing someone, I don't think that the death penalty would necessarily detter them anymore than a life sentence.  I helped my younger brother with a school project on this subject awhile back.  As we were researching certian details, we came across some revealing statistics.  I don't have them on hand, but I'll tell you this.  Records of crimes(murders) committed where the death penalty was not issued were not any higher than those who where using the death penalty.  I viewed many studies on this, and all showed that the death penalty is statistically not any more of a deterent than a life sentance.  Maybe I'll do some digging and see if I can find those stats....<P>||||reg||1
