Z||000068||Fierowrecker||09-12-2001||10:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Boomtastic:<BR><B> Actually, I disagree. Let's look at it this way - why don't you or I kill people? We are afraid of the consequences that follow when we are caught. If you know about, or care about, the consequences prior to commiting the crime, most people would be hesitant about commiting the crime in the first place.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My deterent isn't any form of punishment man can dish out...<BR>I fear God's punishment...<BR>Thou shalt not kill...<BR>The terrorists believe they will go straight to heaven as soon as they die for killing infidels (Christians, Americans, Saitan's spawn, whatever) and so they don't fear dieing or commiting suicide missions, as did the hijackers...<BR>They believe they will be martyrs if they die while killing for God...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
